==Freedom of panorama== <!--T:32-->
</translate>
<noinclude>{{CRT shortcut|FOP|Thailand}}</noinclude>
<translate>
<!--T:33-->
{{OkMark}} for exterior and interior architecture, and artistic works permanently displayed in public places: {{tlx|FoP-Thailand}}
{{NotMark}} for artistic works ''not'' permanently displayed in public places.

<!--T:34-->
The ''Thai Copyright Act of B.E. 2537 (A.D. 1994)'' states that:
*Any drawing, painting, construction, engraving, sculpting, carving, printing, photography, filmmaking, broadcasting, or any similar act involving any artwork <u>permanently</u> displayed in a public place, other than architectural works, shall not be deemed to infringe copyright on that artwork.
</translate>
<translate>
<!--T:35-->
*A drawing, painting, engraving, moulding, carving, lithographing, photographing, cinematographing or video broadcasting of an architectural work shall not be deemed an infringement of copyright in the architectural work.<tvar name="ref1">{{sref|2537/1994 Sec.38}}</tvar>
For artistic works that are ''not'' situated in public spaces (not "openly located in a public place"), these can only be photographed freely if ''{{pg|Commons:De minimis|de minimis}}'':
*A photograph or cinematograph or video broadcast of <u>a work of which an artistic work is a component</u> shall not be deemed an infringement of copyright in the artistic work.<tvar name="ref2">{{sref|2537/1994 Sec.39}}</tvar>
*Note that ''artistic work'' as defined by Section 4 of the law does not include works of literature. On the other hand, ''architecture'' as defined in the same section includes "design of buildings or constructions, a design of interior or exterior decoration as well as a landscape design or a creation of a model of buildings or constructions." It can be interpreted that elegant bridges are works of architecture that fall under the freedom of panorama, through the element "constructions."

<!--T:70-->
See  <tvar name="1">[[:wikisource:th:พระราชบัญญัติลิขสิทธิ์ พ.ศ. 2537]]</tvar> for the Thai text.
</translate>

